# Headers for STATIC ASSETS only (Workers assets serve these before the
# Worker runs; Worker responses set their own headers in src/worker/index.js).
#
# Icons/cards are re-fetched by scripts/fetch-logos.mjs and not content-hashed,
# so a bounded 7-day cache balances freshness against the ~41 requests per
# cold page view (site-auditor weight.caching finding, 2026-08-04). HSTS
# mirrors the Worker's posture so every /service-status response carries it.
#
# The CSP is for files opened at their own URL: the Worker's nonce policy
# never reaches a static asset, and a vendor SVG is a document. Nothing may
# load or run; inline styles (which real marks use) still apply, embedded
# images are data: only, and `sandbox` gives the document an opaque origin.
# The dashboard shows these through <img>, which this policy does not change.
# fetch-logos.mjs refusing active SVG content is the first layer; this is the
# second. Pinned by test/worker/static-headers.test.js.
/service-status/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=604800
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'none'; img-src 'self' data:; style-src 'unsafe-inline'; frame-ancestors 'none'; sandbox
